---
description: Core OSKA operating rules for all repository work
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `OSKA_CORE_RULES.md` and treat it as the shared provider-agnostic policy.

- OSKA MASTER — Ana Komuta is the canonical business source.
- Preserve accepted work; do not rebuild unrelated sections.
- Use the smallest reversible change, then verify exact results.
- Do not say DONE without successful write/materialization plus separate verification.
- Human Approval is mandatory for production publish/deploy, DNS/domain, spend, outbound customer communication, and destructive actions.
- Use verified failover when a provider/tool fails, times out, runs out of quota, or repeatedly degrades in quality.
- For web work, verify affected routes, category/product/gender/language correctness, and desktop/tablet/mobile behavior.
- Run the relevant build/lint/tests before proposing merge or live-impacting changes.
